[BLAME] benchmark_3/parts/dag_engine/lib/dag_engine_impl.py: [slug:dag.scheduler.next_wave.ready_nodes] [viol:pret_qa.postcondition_divergence] Facet: scheduler state visibility for graph-registered nodes Witness: add_node(node_id='', action=noop_action, dependencies=None, priority=0, timeout_seconds=None, retries=0) followed by get_state(node_id='') which raises KeyError: '' and get_all_states() which yields an empty mapping instead of {'': READY}. WaveScheduler.get_state (lines 335-337) and get_all_states (lines 339-341) read the internal state map without reconciling it against the DAG's registered nodes, while next_wave and is_finished call _sync_states (line 343) first. The specification requires get_all_states to return the execution state of every node in the graph and get_state to report the current state of an existing node; a node registered with no dependencies is READY (consistent with next_wave.ready_nodes), so both accessors must surface READY for node_id='' and a state entry for every registered node rather than raising KeyError or returning a stale, empty mapping. Reconcile the DAG node population inside both accessors before reporting states.
[CHANGE] benchmark_3/parts/dag_engine/lib/dag_engine_impl.py: Reconcile WaveScheduler state map with registered DAG nodes inside get_state and get_all_states so both accessors surface READY for dependency-free nodes and report an entry for every node registered in the DAG instead of raising KeyError or returning a stale empty mapping.
[BLAME] benchmark_3/parts/dag_engine/pretense/dag_engine_pretense.py: [slug:dag.scheduler.mark_succeeded.promote_dependents] [viol:pret_qa.overspecified_oracle] Facet: node readiness under late prerequisite edge Witness: add_node(node_id='', action=noop_action, dependencies=None, priority=0, timeout_seconds=None, retries=0), add_edge(upstream_id='', downstream_id=''), get_state(node_id='') and get_all_states() both fail the ret == current assertion. The interface model derives node readiness only when add_node registers the node (READY if it had no upstream at that instant), and the add_edge transition updates only the upstream/downstream adjacency without reconciling node_states, so a node registered without dependencies and later given a prerequisite retains READY in the model. A dependent must be promoted to READY only once its upstream dependencies have SUCCEEDED, so the model's get_state and get_all_states oracles assert a stale READY that the specification does not require, and the same stale state arises for any later-added prerequisite, not only the self-referential edge in the witness. Reconcile modeled node readiness in the add_edge transition so the model never reports READY for a node with an unsatisfied upstream dependency.
[CHANGE] benchmark_3/parts/dag_engine/pretense/dag_engine_pretense.py: Reconcile modeled node readiness for late prerequisite edges: add_edge demotes a READY dependent to PENDING while any upstream dependency is not SUCCEEDED, and add_node applies the same reconciliation when re-registering a node with new dependencies; added a fake scenario asserting the dependent remains PENDING until its prerequisite SUCCEEDS and becomes READY afterwards.
