[BLAME] benchmark_3/parts/dag_engine/lib/dag_engine_impl.py: [slug:dag.scheduler.mark_failed.fail_fast] [viol:pret_qa.postcondition_divergence] Facet: scheduler state cache lag after graph mutation Witness: pattern one add_node(node_id='', action=noop_action, dependencies=None, priority=0, timeout_seconds=None, retries=0), next_wave(), add_edge(upstream_id='', downstream_id=''), then get_state(node_id='') reports READY where PENDING is required and get_all_states() returns the same stale entry; pattern two add_node(node_id='', action=noop_action, dependencies=None, priority=0, timeout_seconds=None, retries=0), add_node(node_id='0', action=noop_action, dependencies=None, priority=0, timeout_seconds=None, retries=0), mark_failed(node_id='', failure_policy=FAIL_FAST), then next_wave() returns ['0'], is_finished() returns False, and get_all_states() shows node '0' READY instead of CANCELLED. WaveScheduler reconciles its state cache with the DAG only for node identifiers it has not seen before, so the recent reconciliation that made get_state and get_all_states surface registered nodes is insufficient: a node whose state was already cached stays READY when add_edge later registers an unsatisfied prerequisite, and the same registered topology therefore reports READY or PENDING depending on whether the node was queried before the edge was added, contradicting the requirement that get_state report the current execution state. The same partial-cache defect leaves fail_fast incomplete: mark_failed with FAIL_FAST cancels only cached nodes, so a node registered in the DAG but never observed is not transitioned to CANCELLED even though fail_fast requires all remaining unexecuted nodes to be CANCELLED, which makes next_wave return an uncancelled node and is_finished report False when all nodes should be terminal. Derive node states from the current DAG topology on every accessor and apply the fail_fast cancellation across every node registered in the DAG so these observables depend only on the current graph and execution history.
[CHANGE] benchmark_3/parts/dag_engine/lib/dag_engine_impl.py: Derive WaveScheduler states from current DAG topology on every sync: newly visible nodes become READY only when prerequisites are satisfied, cached READY nodes are demoted to PENDING when a new edge adds an unsatisfied prerequisite, and cached PENDING nodes are promoted to READY once all prerequisites succeed. Reconcile all registered DAG nodes inside mark_failed before applying policies so FAIL_FAST cancels every remaining non-terminal node, and inside mark_succeeded before unlocking dependents.
