[CHANGE] benchmark_3/parts/dag_engine/pretense/dag_engine_impl_pretense.py: Broaden contract coverage in the real implementation suite: added degenerate-graph scenarios (empty DAG queries, empty critical path via raw SUT), removal-with-dependents and prerequisite-removal readiness, late-prerequisite readiness, already-non-pending dependent promotion, blocked-wave termination, transitive skip diamond, retry failure accounting, and explicit contract-violation/recovery scenarios for NodeNotFoundError (add_edge/remove_node/get_node/get_dependencies/get_dependents/validate), CycleError (validate/topological_sort), DAGTimeoutError (run timeout) and DAGCancelledError (cancel during execution).
[BLAME] benchmark_3/parts/dag_engine/pretense/dag_engine_pretense.py: [slug:dag.scheduler.next_wave.ready_nodes] [viol:pret_qa.uncontracted_state_rule] Facet: node readiness derivation at registration and removal Witness: (1) add_node(node_id='', action=noop_action, dependencies=None, priority=-240, timeout_seconds=None, retries=1), add_node(node_id='x', action=failing_action, dependencies=None, priority=589, timeout_seconds=300.0, retries=1), mark_succeeded(node_id='x'), add_node(node_id='0', action=value_action, dependencies=['x'], priority=-3342847, timeout_seconds=300.0, retries=0), then get_all_states() leaves node '0' PENDING while the scheduler reports READY; (2) add_node(node_id=''), add_node(node_id='0'), add_edge(upstream_id='', downstream_id='0'), remove_node(node_id=''), then next_wave() yields [] while the scheduler yields ['0'], and get_state(node_id='0') reports PENDING while the scheduler reports READY; (3) add_node(node_id='a'), add_node(node_id='b', dependencies=['a']), add_node(node_id='c', dependencies=['a']), remove_node(node_id='a'), then next_wave() yields [] while ['b', 'c'] is required. The model reconciles node readiness only for the late-prerequisite demotion direction handled by the latest change: add_node leaves a node PENDING even when every registered dependency has already SUCCEEDED, and remove_node purges incident edges without promoting dependents that are now unblocked, so modeled node readiness stays stale and the get_state, get_all_states, next_wave and is_finished oracles assert an unready classification the contract does not support. A node whose upstream dependencies have all SUCCEEDED, and a node left with no upstream dependencies after incident edge removal, must be classified READY so that next_wave reports it, consistent with the promotion semantics required for newly unblocked dependents. Reconcile modeled readiness in add_node when registered dependencies are already satisfied and in remove_node for dependents whose remaining prerequisites are satisfied.
[CHANGE] benchmark_3/parts/dag_engine/pretense/dag_engine_pretense.py: Reconcile modeled node readiness in both directions: a shared _reconcile_readiness helper classifies any non-terminal node as READY exactly when all of its upstream dependencies are SUCCEEDED (so add_node classifies nodes registered with already-satisfied prerequisites as READY, and add_edge handles both demotion and promotion). remove_node now records direct dependents before purging incident edges and reclassifies each of them afterwards, so dependents left with no remaining prerequisites become READY and are reported by next_wave/get_state/get_all_states. Added a fake readiness-derivation scenario covering registration with a satisfied prerequisite and promotion after prerequisite removal.
